n the fullness  of their love and it just doesn't  track because the show never properly  grapples  with just how one-sided their  relationship actually  is given that i've  just touched on the end of series 8 i  feel like this is a good time to address  how many times clara was set up to exit  the show and then  just didn't starts with a fantastic  scene where the doctor and clara both  lie to each other and then they part  ways  neither in a state where they are able  to continue journeying  with the other and it has been confirmed  that this was originally written as an  exit point for clara though before  production started  jenna coleman decided to stay on board  this would be the first of  two times that she would almost leave  the show  as then last christmas was also written  as her exit only to have her change her  mind and stay after the table read  now this i'm ready to leave no  wait i'll stay thing especially twice in  a row  is pretty much the one item that i'm  going to hold  jenna coleman culpable for and all this  now if this had happened in an american  show  it would have been a very safe bet that  the actor was just saying they're  leaving in order  to try and squeeze out a pay increase in  order to keep them around but  tv production culture in the uk isn't  really the same  beast and i never got that impression  and i  do believe that she really did genuinely  feel torn about leaving  and changed her mind which  okay that happens  but it still does have a tangible impact  on the show  death in heaven felt largely unaltered  it really did read like they just kept  the she's not coming back script  as it already was since the ending  wasn't quite so firm that they couldn't  in fact roll it back and have a return  and have her return and appear again  last christmas on the other hand is a  bit of  a mess toward the end now stephen moffat  claims he wrote two versions right from  the start  suspecting she might change her mind  again and to be honest  i have a really hard time believing that  because after a really well done  heartfelt resolution to clara's time  with the doctor and giving her a full  life without him  the no wait she's fine more adventures  ending  feels nothing if not stapled on after  the fact  and the thing is i'm actually trying to  be nice to moffitt when i say i don't  believe him about always having a  version  ready to go where she stays because  if that's not true and he didn't always  have it it would definitely explain why  it feels like it ends twice  with the second ending added on as  quickly as possible without altering the  rest of the script  but if it's true and he always did have  this one plan then honestly  it means he thought it was better to  fake out and exit and backtrack  immediately rather than do a proper  rework  so that the ending where she stays feels  organic and not tacked on and that is  just  terrible writing and even if i set that  aside and don't get hung up on how weird  and disjointed  the end of last christmas feels this is  still a problem  because it inherently devalues the  tension that would otherwise be inherent  when she actually leaves  you can't keep faking out the audience  and expect the same  impact every day in time is why  character deaths carry no weight in  superhero comics  fool us once shame on you fool us twice  shame on us  try and fool us the same way over and  over and over and over again  how stupid you think i am but okay so  after an undercooked first series but a  stronger yet still flawed second series  with two good exits that didn't turn out  to be exits  we finally got the actual real no  fingers crossed we promise  final series for clara oswald series  nine now here's the thing  series nine nearly won me over on clara  actually i tell a lie series nine did in  fact win me over  it just then lost me again with an  episode that i am going to spend  as little time as humanly possible on  because i've already devoted  three vi