ly  as a snippet that could be used in  teasers but  now retroactively it becomes something  that is stoking the fire  of her drive to measure up to the doctor  and do the things that he would do  it's a really smart thing to latch onto  so that now  she has a trajectory and a path that  leads to her debt that doesn't feel  unearned or manufactured  the hints are there and they exist in  the previous series now  that she is always on the path to face  the raven it's brought up again  in series nine and under the lake where  the doctor flat out tells her  to not try and be him  and ultimately that's the very thing  that gets her killed  trying to out think the situation doing  what she believes the doctor would do  that is why she died she is so sure that  she is doing the smart thing  certain enough that it's what the doctor  would do she doesn't even  think that she needs to tell him before  she does it  and then she dies from that choice  it's a choice that's built up to it's  treated as a tragedy rather than karmic  retribution  it's unfair but not unprovoked  she didn't deserve this but she still  brought it on herself  and the fact that it happens not in the  finale but with two episodes still to go  was the perfect way to defuse the issue  of two previous near exits  because it swoops in ahead of when fans  would have been prepared for it  adding to the tragedy and the impact of  the whole thing it is  borderline genius  which is ultimately undermined two  episodes later with hell bent and rather  than rehash my issues you can check out  my last video i made on it there's the  thing only bit i want to add on  the topic of that episode is that i know  i know there are people who truly love  hell bent  part of that does seem to depend on how  they feel about clara as a character  people who loved the character even  before that episode airs  do tend to be hell bent defenders  additionally i am aware that some people  feel that i  fundamentally misunderstand not 